{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1473408005,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNzU5NTAzMDA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/776","origin":"github"},"title":"Should `save auto_add_changes` default to True?","message":"As we are moving to a paradigm where every datalad action (bundle) results in a commit, the only changes left are likely user-made modifications outside datalad command. It would make sense to me to set the default to `True`, because in all likelihood users want to save all those changes.\n\nIn order to keep the `files` parameter useful and functional. We could fail when `-a` _and_ `files` are given. This would yield the ability to save individual bits, but also to save all at once by default.","files":null}]}